  "summary": "The paper fabricated nine distinct Ti3C2Tx AMX electrode materials by varying the number of MXene infiltration/deposition cycles (4D\u201320D) and/or compressing the AMX-8D framework from 2000 to 50 \u00b5m. All used LiF/HCl MILD-derived, delaminated Ti3C2Tx assembled on sacrificial tetrapodal ZnO templates and tested in 0.5 M H2SO4. AMX-20D-200 is the most plausible headline high-areal-loading electrode, with 7.2 mg cm\u22122 loading and the study\u2019s ~1.4 F cm\u22122 at 200 mV s\u22121; however, the text does not explicitly assign that headline value to a label. AMX-16D-200 explicitly delivered 261 F g\u22121 at 20 A g\u22121, while AMX-8D-50 reached 180 F cm\u22123 at 50 mV s\u22121 and was used in the symmetric device. BET area, pore-size distributions, tortuosity, and per-sample porosity were generally not reported."
